cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use Apus, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
title: 'Apus: lidar-based bird-flight monitoring'
abstract: >-
  Apus turns raw lidar returns into bird tracks with deterministic, explainable
  methods (background modelling, connected components, IMM-Kalman tracking and
  explicit rules) and runs them through a data platform that produces
  detectability-corrected passage rates, flight-height distributions,
  weather-radar comparisons and collision-risk estimates.
authors:
  - family-names: Mohammadpour
    given-names: Soheil
repository-code: https://github.com/soheil-mp/apus
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - lidar
  - point cloud
  - ornithology
  - bird migration
  - multi-target tracking
  - collision risk
  - data engineering
